* S3 bucket versioning
>> Provide security against accidental  deletion of object/data  or overwrite. 
>> Versioning can be also used for data retention and archive. 
>> once you enable versioning on bucket, it can't be disabled however it can be suspended. 
>> When enabled , bucket versioning will protect existing and new object and maintain their version as they are updated. 
>> when you try to delete an object, a delete marker is placed. 
>> you can still view the object and delete marker. 
>> You will be charged for all S3 storage cost for all object version stored. 
>> YOu can used S3 lifecycle policies to delete older vsersion or you can move them to cheaper S3 storage or glacier. 
>> Bucket version state
  -- Enabled 
  -- suspended.
>> versioning applies to all object in a bucket and not partially applied. 
>> Object existed before versioning remain version id will be NULL. 
>> If versioning is suspended , existed object and their version remain as it. New version will not be created. New id will be null. 
>> If same key is used to store another object , it will override the existing one. 
>> Object deletion in suspended , then once object with Null ID will be deleted. 

* Multifactor authentication : 
>> It delete versioning capacity that adds another level of security in case your account is compromised. 
>> It add another layer of security for the following : 
  -- changing your bucket versioning
  -- Permanently deleting  object version. 
 >> MFA delete require 
   -- Your security credentials. 
   -- The code displayed on approved physical of software based authentication device. 
   
   
** S3 multiport upload 
>> It upload a object in parts.. parts are uploaded independently and in paralleled , in any order. but it is stored at one place. 
>> recommended for the object sizes of 100 MB or larger. 
>> It must used for object larger than 5GB
>> It is done through multiport upload API.

** Copying S3 object. 
>> It create a copy of an object that is already stored in Amazon S3. 
>> can create a copy of your object upto 5GB in single atomic operation. if more than 5GB then use multiport upload API. 
>> Incur ,if copy to another region.
>> Use the copy operation to 
   -- Generate additional copies of subject. 
   -- Renaming object. 
   -- Move object across AWS location/region. 
   -- Change object metadata. 
   
