* EBS encryption 
>> EBS encryption is supported on all EBS volume type and all EC2 instance families 
>> Snapshot of encrypted volume are also encrypted.
>> Data encryption at rest means , encryption data while it is stored on the data storage device. 
>>Different methods to encrypt data on EBS Volums 
   --use third party EBS volume
   --Encryption tools 
   --use encrypted EBS
   -- Use encryption at the OS level 
   -- Encrypt data at the application level before storing it at the volume.
>> Encrypted volume are accessed exactly like unencrypted onces, basically encryption is handled transparently. 
>> You can attach an encrypted and unencrypted volumes to the EC2 instance.
Note: encryption is done at EC2 level, then data is stored at EBS volume,
>> EBS volume are not physically attached to the EC2 instance.It is virtually attached. 
>> Data in transit between EC2 and encrypted EBS volume is also encrypted.
>> There is no direct way to change the encryption state of the volume. 
----> to change the state  of encryption ( indirectly ) of non root volume  you need to follow following ways
     >> Attach a new encrypted EBS volume to EC2 instance that has the data to be encrypted then, 
	 >> Mount the new volume to EC2 instance .
	 >> Copy the data from un-encrypted volume to new volume. 
	 >> Both volumes must be on the same EC2 instance. 
	 note: while adding new volume we can enable the encryption options for new volume. 
----> second method for encrytion 
      >> Create a snapshot of the unencryted volume. 
	  >> copy the snapshot and choose  the encrytion for the new copy, this will create encryted copy of snapshot. 
	  >> use this new copy to create an EBS volume, which will be encryted too. 
	  >> Attach the new encrypted EBS volume to the EC2 instance. 
** to change encrytion of EBS Volume for root volume 
Note : There is no way to encrypt the root volume at the time of it's creation. 
 >> There is no direct wa to change the encrytion state of a volume. 
 >> There is indirect workaround
    -- Lauch the instance with EBS volume requried. 
	--Create an AMI from EC2 instance 
	-- copy the AMI and choose encrytion while copying. 
	-- this result it an encrypted AMI that is private. 
	-- Use encrypted AMI to launch new EC2 instance which will have their EBS root volulme encypted. 
 
 
